"op","op":"minus","args":[{"k":"real","v":1},{"k":"op","op":"div","args":[{"k":"op","op":"pow","args":[{"k":"id","name":"π"},{"k":"real","v":2}]},{"k":"op","op":"mult","args":[{"k":"real","v":2},{"k":"op","op":"pow","args":[{"k":"id","name":"n"},{"k":"real","v":2}]}]}]}]}]},"global":false,"stored":null,"unit":null,"shown":false}},{"id":"24","left":54,"top":1010,"alignX":54,"alignY":1010,"disabled":false,"content":{"k":"plot","x":null,"ys":[{"k":"id","name":"P"}],"markers":false,"width":230,"height":190,"xAxis":{"min":null,"max":null,"log":false},"yAxis":{"min":null,"max":null,"log":false},"view":"surface"}},{"id":"25","left":306,"top":1010,"alignX":306,"alignY":1010,"disabled":false,"content":{"k":"plot","x":null,"ys":[{"k":"id","name":"P"}],"markers":false,"width":230,"height":190,"xAxis":{"min":null,"max":null,"log":false},"yAxis":{"min":null,"max":null,"log":false},"view":"contour"}},{"id":"27","left":54,"top":1261,"alignX":54,"alignY":1277,"disabled":false,"content":{"k":"eval","expr":{"k":"op","op":"indexer","args":[{"k":"id","name":"P"},{"k":"real","v":8},{"k":"real","v":8}]},"stored":null,"unit":null}}],"texts":[{"id":"1","left":54,"top":72,"width":440,"height":27,"text":"Heat in a rod and a plate: two partial differential equations, one changing in time and one at rest."},{"id":"2","left":54,"top":107,"width":440,"height":54,"text":"A metal rod 1 m long, hot in the middle, its ends held at 0 °C in ice water. Its temperature u(x, t) obeys the heat equation, u_t = α·u_xx, with α its thermal diffusivity. Typed between Given and Pdesolve, as written: the subscripts are typed after a . so they read as literal subscripts."},{"id":"13","left":54,"top":559,"width":440,"height":27,"text":"At 0, 2, 6 and 20 seconds: the sharp peak spreads out and sinks as heat leaves through the ends. The middle's temperature over time:"},{"id":"17","left":54,"top":632,"width":440,"height":27,"text":"In the long run only the slowest shape is left, a sine, dying as e^(−απ²t): from 6 s to 20 s by a factor of about e^(−0.01·π²·14) = 0.25, as the answers show."},{"id":"18","left":54,"top":864,"width":440,"height":54,"text":"A square plate, one edge (row 0 of the grid) held at 100 °C and the other three at 0 °C, at rest: Laplace's equation, ∇²T = 0. On a 17 × 17 grid each point is the average of its four neighbours, a·T(i+1, j) + b·T(i−1, j) + c·T(i, j+1) + d·T(i, j−1) + e·T(i, j) = 0 with a to d 1 and e −4; relax solves it from the edges inward."},{"id":"26","left":54,"top":1226,"width":440,"height":27,"text":"The heat reaches in from the hot edge; the centre of the plate settles at a quarter of the edge's temperature, 25 °C, as symmetry says it must:"},{"id":"28","left":54,"top":1299,"width":440,"height":27,"text":"rjac, 1 − π²/(2n²), sets how hard each sweep over-relaxes; this value suits an n × n grid. multigrid solves the same equation with a source and zero edges faster still."}],"opaque":[],"origin":0,"tol":0.001,"exactCompare":true,"zeroOverZero":false,"otherRegions":{},"componentOutputs":[]}}